  message: "Phase A shipped in commit f1f992e01e on branch jgstern-agent/refactor/wi-mugog-url-folding-yaml-substrate (auto-pr in flight). Behavior-preserving refactor: `_fold_template_literal` (WI-sijoh JS/TS) and `_fold_elm_string_join` (WI-rosan Elm) extracted out of `linkers/http.py` into engines in new package `hypergumbo_core/url_folding/`, with per-idiom YAML registry (`string_interpolation.yaml` covers {javascript, typescript} via `fold_string_interpolation`; `array_join.yaml` covers {elm} via `fold_array_join`) and `SCOPE.md` documenting Phase-A literal-only languages (python, go, ruby, java). Legacy function names retained as one-line thin wrappers — zero behavior change on canonical pipeline, 197/197 existing test_http_linker.py tests pass unchanged, full smart-test 5457/5457 pass, all 5 packages at 100% coverage in isolation. Dispatcher helper (`_apply_url_folding_yaml`) deferred to Phase B per AGENTS.md anti-premature-abstraction discipline — Elm's two-pass let-binding scan would force a special-case branch from day one with only 2 variants in flight. Property test `test_active_route_languages_are_covered_or_scoped` is the future-proof coverage gate: any new active route-detector language added to the suffix-dispatch table must be YAML-covered or SCOPE.md-scoped, hard fail otherwise. INV-miloj closure criterion is NOT met by Phase A alone — sibling Phase B (Python f-strings + Kotlin/Ruby/Scala/Swift interpolation), Phase C (printf_format), and Phase D (string_concat) are still outstanding under the parent invariant. No bakeoff claim → no awaits_bakeoff_validation tag."  # e029
